        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "de856a4f-85cf-5bb9-81b5-6673ef78e623",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game\n- Places: BB&T Center, Sunrise, Florida\n- Organizations: National Hockey League, Florida Panthers\n\nFacts:\n- The BB&T Center in Sunrise, Florida, was completed in 1998 at a cost of US$185 million and was almost entirely publicly financed.\n- The BB&T Center features 70 suites and 2,623 club seats.\n- The indoor arena now called the BB&T Center was previously known as the National Car Rental Center, Office Depot Center, and BankAtlantic Center.\n- The 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game was held during the 2002–03 NHL season on February 2, 2003.\n- The 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game took place at the Office Depot Center in Sunrise, Florida, which was the home arena of the Florida Panthers.",
